From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 15:12:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] asap7: let a design set DONT_USE_CELLS
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The platform assigned DONT_USE_CELLS with `=` after the design's config
was read, so a design's own list was silently replaced by the platform's
and never reached synthesis or the resizer. A design that brings in LVT
and SLVT (ASAP7_USE_VT) and wants synthesis to stay on RVT cannot say so.
The platform's list is now the default; SDF* and ICG* are still appended
either way.

Not upstreamed. Retires on the //:bump onto an ORFS that carries it.

Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
 flow/platforms/asap7/config.mk | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/flow/platforms/asap7/config.mk b/flow/platforms/asap7/config.mk
--- a/flow/platforms/asap7/config.mk
+++ b/flow/platforms/asap7/config.mk
@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@
 
 # Dont use cells to ease congestion
 # Specify at least one filler cell if none
-export DONT_USE_CELLS          = *x1p*_ASAP7* *xp*_ASAP7*
+export DONT_USE_CELLS          ?= *x1p*_ASAP7* *xp*_ASAP7*
 export DONT_USE_CELLS          += SDF* ICG*
 
 export SYNTH_MINIMUM_KEEP_SIZE       ?= 1000
